  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FTF Bangladesh USAID&#x2019;s Leaving No One Behind Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  Mission Aviation Fellowship (MAF) flight services will continue to support USAID and its partner agencies to access hard-to-reach areas in Bangladesh, safely and efficiently ensuring that development interventions benefit everyone, including those in remote areas who are usually the most vulnerable.  In Bangladesh, many areas that are prone to poverty and climate change are difficult to access on foot and as such, aerial photographs are vital to study and map them.  This activity will include an aerial survey facility to support USAID decision-making by providing easily accessible GPS tagged aerial photographs over vulnerable and high-risk areas.  These aerial surveys will also include locations to assist USAID and its partners in documenting the impact of slow-onset events such as riverbank erosion and waterlogging to help chart population movements, loss of agricultural land, etc.  Through chartered and shuttle flights, MAF will continue its flight services to all development and humanitarian agencies working to save human life and improve the livelihoods of vulnerable people in Bangladesh.  MAF flight services will help increase the chances of aid agencies accessing hard-to-reach areas towards ensuring that no one is left behind.  MAF will contribute to activity monitoring oversight, needs assessment, joint missions with other development partners and private sector organizations where it is hard to reach.  It will provide flight services to anywhere in Bangladesh where commercial flights are unavailable or multiple vehicles are necessary to reach, and will continue to focus on the areas of emergency and disaster responses, food security, climate change, natural resource management, energy, health, education, and population.  In addition, MAF services may contribute to emergency services for medical supplies, including COVID test kits and lab reagents and for training of service providers in remote public health facilities.. .</narrative>
  </description>
